      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1869 a normal school opened in Carbondale, later renamed Southern Illinois University in 1947, turning the city into a college town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Carbondale-Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city hosts the annual Big Muddy Film Festival each February and March, drawing filmmakers and audiences from across the country.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
